<p>The grandfather entered walking easily and without crutches. His eye was clear, his hearing good, and he spoke distinctly.</p>
<p>He looked at the grain, turned it about in his hand, bit a piece off and tasted it. He said it was the very same kind.</p>
<div class="exam"><b>🎯 Most Important:</b> The grandfather could recognise the grain because he had seen and lived on such grain in his young days.</div>
