<div class="card"><b>🤝 Sharing</b><p>People grew their own corn and shared when there was need.</p></div>
<div class="card"><b>💰 Money</b><p>They knew nothing of money.</p></div>
</div>
<div class="quote">“Each man had corn enough of his own.”</div>
<p>The King asked where the grandfather’s field was. His answer: his field was God’s earth; wherever he ploughed, there was his field. Land was free and no man called it his own. Labour was the only thing men called their own.</p>
<div class="visual">
<div class="flow"><div class="node">God’s earth</div><div class="arrow">→</div><div class="node">Free land</div><div class="arrow">→</div><div class="node">Labour was one’s own</div></div>
