<span class="sectionno">17</span>
<h2>Writing — Answer in About Fifty Words</h2>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card">
<p><b>1.</b> How did the grain of corn reach the King?</p>
<p><b>Answer:</b> Some children found the unusual grain in a ravine. A traveller saw it, bought it from them for a penny, took it to town and sold it to the King as a curiosity.</p>
</div>
<div class="card">
<p><b>2.</b> How did the wise men know that it was a grain of corn?</p>
<p><b>Answer:</b> The wise men could not identify it. When it lay on a window-sill, a hen pecked at it and made a hole. Then everyone saw that it was a grain of corn.</p>
</div>
<div class="card">
<p><b>3.</b> What suggestion did the learned men give?</p>
<p><b>Answer:</b> They searched their books but found nothing. They suggested that the King should ask the peasants, perhaps some had heard from their fathers when and where grain grew to such a size.</p>
</div>
<div class="card">
<p><b>4.</b> What were the replies of the old peasant and his father?</p>
<p><b>Answer:</b> The first old peasant had never sown, reaped or bought such grain and asked the King to question his father. His father also had not seen such grain but said grain in his time was larger and yielded more flour than present-day grain.</p>
