<section class="slide">
<span class="sectionno">18</span>
<h2>Writing — Continued</h2>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card">
<p><b>5.</b> How were the three old men described?</p>
<p><b>Answer:</b> The first was old and bent, ashy pale and toothless and used two crutches. His father used one crutch and could still see. The grandfather walked without crutches, had clear eyes, good hearing, sound teeth and distinct speech.</p>
</div>
<div class="card">
<p><b>6.</b> Briefly describe the lifestyle during grandfather’s time.</p>
<p><b>Answer:</b> Corn grew everywhere. People grew and harvested their own corn, shared when needed, knew nothing of money, and did not buy or sell bread. The land was free and labour was the only thing men called their own.</p>
</div>
<div class="card">
<p><b>7.</b> What comments did the grandfather give on today’s lifestyle?</p>
<p><b>Answer:</b> He said people had ceased to live by their own labour and had begun depending on the labour of others. In the old time they lived according to God’s law and did not covet what others had produced.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div class="exam"><b>🎯 Exam strategy:</b> Keep answers focused on the events, descriptions and statements actually given in the lesson.</div>
</section>

